#!/usr/bin/env python3
# pro1x-camera-app — a camera for the F(x)tec Pro¹x on libcamera
#
# Photos: the viewfinder is scaled from the photo's own sensor mode (the
# rear's 12 MP, the front's whole array), beside a raw stream of the same
# frames; the shutter keeps the newest raw frame and pro1x-develop turns it
# into a JPEG in ~/Pictures/Camera, the viewfinder running on (RAW).  The
# rear 48 MP, or a failed raw stream, switch libcamerasrc to the photo's
# mode for one frame and back (moWerk's "small viewfinder, photo at full
# resolution", jolla-camera on SailfishOS).  Tap: focus and exposure there
# (af-windows, mapped to pixel array coordinates as moWerk's camerabin
# patch does; spot metering).  Manual focus with a slider.  Shape and
# resolution of what is saved, for photos (16:9, 4:3, 1:1; the sensor's
# own pixels, binned, or half) and for videos (16:9, 4:3; 1080p, 720p),
# kept per camera and mode; the viewfinder shows the same part of the
# scene.  White balance automatic or locked.
# ISO (manual analogue gain, or auto), exposure compensation, the white
# LED as flash (off, on, auto, torch), a 3 or 10 s timer, digital zoom (a
# pinch, or 1x, 2x, 4x), front and rear cameras.  Video mode: H.264 on the
# phone's encoder with the microphone, in ~/Videos/Camera.
# The frames turn with the panel.  SIGUSR1 presses the shutter (the camera
# button, pro1x-camera).
#
# Why not Snapshot: it reads PipeWire's 1080p stream, sets no focus, ISO
# or exposure, and takes no stills (author, 2026-11-01).  Why not moWerk's
# Qt patches: they target SailfishOS's Qt 5.6 fork (9 of 14 do not apply
# to Qt 5.15).  The controls come from libcamera with moWerk's patches
# (libcamera-pro1x).
#
# State: photos, focus, ISO and flash used on the phone since 2026-11-02.
# Flash modes, timer, zoom presets, video and the button rows: used by the
# author on 2026-11-16.  Then rewritten, not yet run in the app: pinch (raw
# touches), recording into the running viewfinder (its pipeline tested
# headless, two recordings closed cleanly), focus held in auto mode, manual
# focus, spot exposure, photo shapes; the 4:3 viewfinder mode and the white
# balance lock (2026-11-16, need the new kernel and libcamera).  Photos from
# the raw stream (2026-11-17): rear 12 MP tested in the app (frame 0.02 s
# after the shutter, saved at 1.3 s), front only headless and in the dark;
# Night and flash with it not yet run.

